{"name":"Bluebottle","hex":"#8ecfe8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bluebottle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cornflower, a plant that grows in grain fields, Centaurea cyanus.","Any of various blowflies of the genus Calliphora that have an iridescent metallic-blue body and make a loud buzzing noise when flying."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marine jellyfish of the genus Physalia, which includes Physalia physalis, the Portuguese man-of-war, and Physalia utriculus, the Pacific man-of-war; a man-of-war."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bluebottle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calliphoridae","blocks":[{"text":"The Calliphoridae are a family of insects in the order Diptera, with almost 1,900 known species. The maggot larvae, often used as fishing bait, are known as gentles. The family is known to be polyphyletic, but much remains disputed regarding proper treatment of the constituent taxa, some of which are occasionally accorded family status."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Chrysomya_megacephala_male.jpg/330px-Chrysomya_megacephala_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calliphoridae","wikidata":"Q28404"},{"title":"Calliphora vomitoria","blocks":[{"text":"Calliphora vomitoria, known as the bluebottle fly, orange-bearded bluebottle, or bottlebee, is a species of blowfly, a species in the family Calliphoridae. Calliphora vomitoria is the type species of the genus Calliphora. It is common throughout many continents including Europe, Americas, and Africa. They are fairly large flies, nearly twice the size of the housefly, with a metallic blue abdomen and long orange setae on the gena."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Calliphora-vomitoria-Bluebottle-fly-20100806a.jpg/330px-Calliphora-vomitoria-Bluebottle-fly-20100806a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calliphora_vomitoria","wikidata":"Q1141108"},{"title":"Bluebottle (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluebottle is a comedy character from The Goon Show, a 1950s British comedy radio show. The character was created and performed by Peter Sellers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebottle_(character)","wikidata":"Q3573973"},{"title":"Bluebottle (uncrewed surface vessels)","blocks":[{"text":"The Bluebottle is an Australian long-range, extra-large unmanned surface vehicle being jointly developed by OCIUS Technology and the Australian Department of Defence (DoD) for the Royal Australian Navy (RAN). 15 have been developed and used by the Royal Australian Navy from 2022-2026 with an additional 40 ordered in March 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/BluebottleUSV.jpg/330px-BluebottleUSV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebottle_(uncrewed_surface_vessels)","wikidata":"Q138798989"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg/500px-Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg/1280px-Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg/500px-Blowfly%2C_Calliphora_erythrocephala%2C_lava.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Larva of Calliphora erythrocephala. The exoskeleton is about 16.5mm long. The mouth hooks are the dark objects on the left","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlowfly%2C_Calliphora_